{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-style Shift-click: extends the current edit selection to the mouse position. The selection is one time range shared by a set of tracks.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Only grows, never shrinks. Clicking before the range extends its start, clicking after it extends its end, clicking inside it keeps the time range as it is. \u8226 ? Tracks: only the clicked track is added (like Cmd-click in Pro Tools); tracks in between are not. Every track of the selection gets the same, extended time range. \u8226 ? The current selection is read from the existing razor areas (all tracks, union of their time ranges). Without razor areas: time selection + selected tracks. Without those: the edit cursor + the selected tracks (or the last touched track). \u8226 ? REAPER clears razor areas when an item is clicked, before this action runs. With "Toggle Track and Razor Item Link like Pro Tools" running, the last razor area is remembered, so Shift-click on an item keeps the original tracks (used only while the time selection still equals that razor range). \u8226 ? Clicking an item extends the range to cover the whole item (to its start or end). Clicking empty track space extends to the mouse position, following snap / grid settings. \u8226 ? The edit cursor does not move. \u8226 ? Track-level razor areas only; envelope-lane razor areas are kept but not extended. \u8226 ? Options inside the script: also set the time selection, the track selection and the item selection to the result.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Suggested setup (suggestions only \u8212- nothing is assigned automatically): Preferences > Editing Behavior > Mouse Modifiers > Track > Left click > Shift, and Media item bottom half (or Media item) > Left click > Shift (Action list...).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Credits: Inspired by Daniel Kharrat's "Extend razor edit area to mouse cursor (select tracks in between)". Designed and tested by hsuanice; code written with Claude Code (AI).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Single-button toggle watcher that add-selects media items on each track according to that track's TRACK-LEVEL Razor Areas (GUID == ""). Envelope-lane razors are preserved but ignored for matching.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODE (user option inside the script): \u8226 ? RANGE_MODE = 1 \u8594 ? Overlap : item is selected if it INTERSECTS any Razor range \u8226 ? RANGE_MODE = 2 \u8594 ? Contain : item is selected only if it is FULLY inside a Razor range (INCLUSIVE with tiny EPS tolerance, so equal-length is selected; Pro Tools-like)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Add-only selection (does not clear existing item selection unless STRICT_SYNC = true). \u8226 ? Does not modify Razor Areas; only reads them. \u8226 ? Relaunching terminates the previous instance and keeps a toolbar toggle in sync.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note: This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Toggle (background watcher). After a right-button DRAG, on the frame the button is released (optionally one frame later) the time selection is set to the earliest start / latest end of the currently selected items. Optimized for large projects: a single pass over the selected items on release (no GUID table, no before/after diff), and an optional skip when the time selection would not change. Requires hsuanice_Mouse.lua (hsuanice Library) and the js_ReaScriptAPI extension.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
