{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 hsuanice Scripts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER scripts for audio post-production, by hsuanice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Install {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab In REAPER: {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories...} and paste:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/hsuanice/ReaScripts/raw/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Browse packages}, search for {\f1 hsuanice}, and install:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b hsuanice Library} (required by most scripts below; adds nothing to the Action List)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab any of the packages listed under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#packages"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Packages
}}}
\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b ReaImGui} \u8212- needed by the GUI scripts; install with ReaPack ({\i ReaTeam Extensions} repository, included by default).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b SWS Extension} \u8212- optional; a few features use it (e.g. {\i Retain Glue Cues}, Session Fix's Off grid).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b js_ReaScriptAPI} \u8212- needed by {\i Toggle Set Time Selection to Items on Right Drag}, recommended for {\i Toggle Track and Razor Item Link like Pro Tools}; install with ReaPack ({\i ReaTeam Extensions}).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Python 3 + OpenTimelineIO} ({\f1 pip install opentimelineio}) \u8212- only for {\i Conform List Browser} AAF / XML / OTIO import; EDL needs nothing extra. AAF also needs {\b aaftool} from LibAAF.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b BWF MetaEdit} ({\f1 bwfmetaedit} command-line tool) \u8212- optional; only needed for timecode (BWF TimeReference) embedding.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Moving from hsuanice/PublicBeta\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository replaces {\f1 hsuanice/PublicBeta}, which is no longer updated. Both install to the same folder, so remove PublicBeta first:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Manage repositories}, right-click {\b hsuanice Scripts} (PublicBeta) > {\b Uninstall}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Import this repository and install the packages as above.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Packages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Script names follow one pattern so they are easy to find in the Action List: the series or package name comes first ({\f1 Hover Editing - ...}, {\f1 Auto Color - ...}), abbreviations are kept next to the full name ({\f1 Conform List Browser - CLB ...}), and background on/off scripts start with {\f1 Toggle}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Renamed on 2026-10-12.} Every script got a clearer name. If you installed an earlier version, reinstall the packages from ReaPack and re-assign your shortcuts / toolbar buttons. The changelog of each package lists the old name.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Rendering\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Render or Glue with Handles - RGWH | Render or glue items with handles (GUI + Glue / Render actions) | | AudioSweet - AudioSuite Workflow | AudioSuite-style offline FX processing, Pro Tools style (GUI + Run / Toggle Preview / Toggle Solo, FX Alias tools) |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Items Editing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Hover Editing | Pro Tools-style Split / Trim at the mouse or edit cursor (Toggle Hover Mode, Split, Trim or Extend Left / Right Edge) | | Reorder - Sort Items Vertically | Vertical reorder and sort of selected items by metadata (GUI + Copy to Sort / Sort in Place / Upfill) | | Session Fix | Session Fix - Interchange Prep: one window that checks and fixes a session before converting it with Interchanger (Pro Tools / Nuendo / Cubase) \u8212- checklist, Fix All, before / after check, review tracks (ReaImGui; replaces the five earlier Session Fix scripts) | | Copy / Cut Items and Envelope Points Respect Razor | Copy or cut items and envelope points, respecting razor edits | | Reposition Items | Space selected items by an interval (GUI) | | Move Selected Items to Track Under Mouse | Move items vertically, keeping their timeline position | | Toggle Mute Item Under Mouse | Mute / unmute the item under the mouse | | Explode Takes Across Tracks | Put each take of the selected items on its own track | | Explode Multichannel Poly Audio to Mono Items | Split poly files into one-channel items, keeping metadata | | Convert Empty Items to Audio Items | Keeps take names and notes | | Copy Unmuted Child Items to Parent Folder Track | Copy unmuted child items to the folder track (checks overlaps first) |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Items Properties\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Auto Color - Items by Take Name | Color items by take-name keywords with a palette (GUI + Toggle Background Coloring, By Palette, Smart Random, Follow Track Color, All Shiny Color) |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Selection\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Toggle Track and Razor Item Link like Pro Tools | Pro Tools-style "Link Track and Edit Selection": tracks follow razor areas / item selection | | Toggle Razor and Item Link Overlap or Contain | Razor areas select the items they overlap or fully contain | | Toggle Set Time Selection to Items on Right Drag | After a right-button drag, the time selection follows the selected items | | Extend Razor Edit to Mouse Cursor like Pro Tools | Pro Tools-style Shift-click: grows the razor area (time range and tracks) to the mouse position, never shrinks it |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Tracks\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Auto Pan LR tracks | Pan adjacent XXX_L / XXX_R track pairs hard left / right | | Delete Selected Tracks with Warning | Safe delete: asks first when tracks have items, FX, routing or are folders | | Show Hide Folder Child Tracks in TCP | Show or hide the children of the selected folder tracks (or of their parent) | | Import Audio Folders to Tracks - Field Recorder | Import one folder per track; channel-split recorder files are grouped (GUI) | | Import Audio Folders to Tracks - Music Multitrack | Import one folder per track for music multitrack sessions (GUI) |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Metadata\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Rename from Metadata | Rename the active take or the source file from BWF / iXML metadata tokens, with live preview (GUI) | | Item List | Spreadsheet-style item tables with metadata columns: Item List Browser - ILB, Item List Editor - ILE (GUI) | | BWF / iXML Embed Tools | Embed BWF iXML Metadata from Take 1, Embed Timecode to BWF and iXML, Embed SMPTE UMID (needs BWF MetaEdit) |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Conform\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Conform List Browser - CLB | Conform tool for EDL / AAF / XML / OTIO / subtitle lists: match source media, generate and link items, compare old / new cuts {\i (compare: work in progress)} (GUI + Jump Old New TC, Link REAPER Items, Load from REAPER, Reveal Item) |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Various\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | Clock with Date 24H | Resizable, dockable clock window | | Count Items and Tracks - Selection HUD | Pro Tools-style selection info: item / track counts, start / end / length |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Library\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | What it does | |---|---| | hsuanice Library | Shared code used by the scripts above; adds nothing to the Action List |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Suggested shortcuts are listed in each package's About page in ReaPack (never assigned automatically).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Pre-release} packages are only offered when {\b Enable pre-releases} is turned on in ReaPack (Extensions > ReaPack > Manage repositories > Options).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Release notes are shown in ReaPack. Older history is in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "Changelogs/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Changelogs/
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Maintaining\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Rules, folder layout and the release workflow are documented in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MAINTAINING.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
MAINTAINING.md
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Built with AI (vibe coding)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 These scripts are a product of {\b vibe coding}: hsuanice is an audio post-production engineer, not a professional programmer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b hsuanice} designs every workflow, decides how each tool should behave, and tests it in real post-production work.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b AI writes most of the code}: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://claude.ai"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Claude
}}}
 by Anthropic and ChatGPT by OpenAI.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Claude Code} (Anthropic's AI coding agent) also helps maintain this repository: the folder structure, ReaPack packaging, version numbers, changelogs and the release workflow.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Please treat the scripts as such: try them on a copy of your project first, and keep backups of media you process. Bug reports and feedback are very welcome \u8212- open an issue on GitHub or reply in the REAPER forum threads linked in each package.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Credits\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The scripts in this repository are designed, tested and maintained by hsuanice, with code written together with AI tools (Claude, ChatGPT).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 AudioSweet is inspired by the AudioSuite-like script by Tim Chimes. "AudioSweet" is a name originally given by Tim Chimes; this project continues to use the name in reference to his original work. Original: "Renders selected plugin to selected media item", written for REAPER 5.1 with Lua (v1.1, 2015-12-22) \u8212- http://timchimes.com/scripting-with-reaper-audiosuite/\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Hover Editing - Toggle Hover Mode is based on / inspired by TJF's {\i Hover Mode Toggle} script.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Extend Razor Edit to Mouse Cursor like Pro Tools is inspired by Daniel Kharrat's {\i Extend razor edit area to mouse cursor (select tracks in between)} script.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Auto Color's palette (hue + per-row saturation / value) is modeled after rodilab's {\i Color palette} script. Auto Color's Shiny mode follows the ShinyColor behavior of {\i Chroma - Coloring Tool} by OLSHALOM \u8212- https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?t=281516\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Session Fix - Interchange Prep's {\i Workflow cues} check takes its way of releasing and reloading media files (media offline / online, rebuild peaks) from amagalma's {\i Remove selected items' active takes' source file cue points (WAV only)} (ReaTeam Scripts).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Conform List Browser uses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
OpenTimelineIO
}}}
 (Academy Software Foundation) for timeline files and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/agfline/LibAAF"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
LibAAF
}}}
 by agfline (aaftool) for AAF. {\f1 Library/json.lua} is based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rxi/json.lua"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
rxi/json.lua
}}}
 (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2020 rxi); the full license notice is kept in the file.\par}
